The default reduces the group of pairs/1 into its count and stores none
of its 36 rows, so it answers under tuples=20.  A strategy that stores the
group -- group-rules, no-group-reduction, or no-magic, which answers from
the whole fixed point without a run's reductions -- passes the limit and
fails, as aggregate-limit.dl pins.  The golden file pins the default's
answer.
